---
title: Andrii Bychkovskyi - Games
description: "Games developed by Andrii Bychkovskyi"
layout: default
---
<style>
  #games {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5em;
    padding: 0 1em;
  }

  .steam-widget {
    width: 646px;
    max-width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 646 / 190;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 4px;

    /* The widget's document body is transparent, so the iframe's own canvas
       shows through around the card. Inheriting `color-scheme: light dark`
       from :root makes that canvas render as an opaque white backdrop, which
       looks fine on the light theme but leaves a white halo in dark mode.
       Resetting to `normal` lets the canvas track the OS scheme like everything
       else, so it stays dark on the dark theme. */
    color-scheme: normal;

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      animation: bounce-appear forwards;
    }
  }
</style>

<div id="games">
  {% for id in games %}
    <iframe
      class="steam-widget"
      src="https://store.steampowered.com/widget/{{ id }}/"
      title="Steam store widget"
      loading="lazy"
      style="animation-duration: {{ forloop.index0 | times: 0.1 | plus: 0.7 }}s;"
    ></iframe>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
